	abstract = {In this description, we introduce a source code analysis tool named Unified CodeCount or UCC developed and maintained by the Center for Systems and Software Engineering at the University of Southern California. UCC is a command-line tool and it has two main features, counting and differencing. With the counting feature, users can generate the physical and logical SLOC counts, and other sizing information including complexity metrics of the target program. The differencing feature allows users to compare and collect the differentials between two versions of the source code, such metrics as the number of added/new, deleted, modified, and unmodified logical SLOC.},
