	abstract = {The necessity of including research and development in economical strategies is greater than ever: Globalization of the market requires a constantly increasing efficiency and speeding up of the entire production process. Since the factor space plays a lesser role nowadays, the apparently endless amount of goods and services on offer cause a constant improvement in quality. Steel industry belongs to the sectors effected most by technological change and globalization of world economy. Steel products are not only produced where they are required but also where this is most economical. Due to its versatile properties steel is a material with a wide range of applications. It will therefore remain a basic material. In order to meet this demand in future, steel industry must make intensive use of research and development. Steel research has been especially developed within the European Union for Coal and Steel (EUCS). The EUCS programme has led to effective activity within the fields of research and development and has achieved much to make European steel industry competitive.},
