	abstract = {The companies in the UK are investing in clean designs that can offset the costs incurred by complying with the RoHS, the Restriction of Hazardous Substances Directive. Giraffe Innovation's Mark Dowling explained that RoHS can have negative effect on all the producers due to energy demands of the alternative solders and the price differential of new solders. Ernst \& Young report has stated that the greatest strategic challenge facing global business in the year 2008. The RoHS directive has put the UK in a better position of responding to forthcoming legislations such as Registration, Evaluation, Authorisation and Restriction of Chemical substances (REACH) and Energy using Products (EuP) as there are new people in the organizations that can respond and engage with the processes. Following a systematic approach to cleaner design can help the companies to identify more efficient designs and production techniques and adopt to major legislations such as RoHS.},
